From: stefanoconiglio <33290924+stefanoconiglio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 02:53:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] page-image also names the source line the page starts
 at

An editor that shows the page beside the source can then bring the source along when the
page is turned.  The line is the first SyncTeX record on the page from one of the
document's own files (an input named relative to it), past the page box; a page with
none (a beamer frame, typeset whole when its \end{frame} is read) gives the place it was
shipped out from.  (page-image PATH PAGE COUNT W H FILE LINE), FILE nil when unknown.
---
